  "not_covered": [
    "Axioms whose object is an anonymous class expression are dropped. OWL restrictions, equivalent-class expressions and union domains and ranges are therefore absent, and a reasoner over these extracts derives less than one over the upstream.",
    "These extracts cannot be used to claim the ontology is consistent with BFO, CCO or BPO. They support the subClassOf reachability the shapes ask about.",
    "BPO is vendored from apqc-ext.ttl and, for the act classes and the one annotation property this repository names, from the additional files its pin lists, each taking only the subjects its pattern matches. BPO's catalog, capabilities_wiring.ttl, delivery_processes.ttl and capability classes are not here (RP-3; Stage 05 standard, section 4).",
    "Specification seeds are read from the draft specification's text. A term it names that no pinned file describes is recorded, not refused: some are terms the BCO will mint, some are BPO terms from unvendored files, and some may be typos. Which is which is not decided here, so they are recorded as the specification writes them and attributed to no namespace: the specification writes ex: for BPO's terms and for the BCO's own, and expanding ex:BusinessCapability under BPO's namespace would attribute a BCO class to BPO.",
    "Only terms this repository names, and their structural ancestry, are present. A new upstream reference in the corpus is not covered until this is rebuilt; tests/test_upstream_vendoring.py fails when that happens.",
    "owl:imports is not emitted. Validation is offline by design, so nothing resolves over the network at check time."
